.resources/TASK-260715-18owh7/TASK-260715-18owh7_inputs.md:1:Resolve the relux-relay protocol-v1 RESOURCE-LIMIT exchange — the numeric limits the binding ADR (TASK-260715-111tde) deferred to this task: max concurrent UDP associations, max queued bytes (per-association + aggregate), max datagram size, idle/association timeout, and hard ceilings; plus WHETHER protocol-v1 EXCHANGES these (client<->relay negotiate an agreed value in the hello/handshake) or each side LOCALLY caps them, and the wire fields if exchanged. Per .spec/relay-protocol.md (protocol-v1) + security-privacy.md (relay validates address families, lengths, association IDs, datagram limits BEFORE opening/using sockets; bounded memory) + the 111tde binding ADR (hello/envelope framing). EVIDENCE-GATE INVARIANT (goal): these are INJECTABLE M0 BASELINES with documented rationale, NOT final tuned values — final tuning is M3 (memory/window/rekey story 1zzt0c + instrumentation 19ii11); pick conservative memory-safe baselines consistent with the iOS ~25-30MB budget (ADR-009) and the HEV UDP-in-TCP path, and keep every value injectable/configurable. DELIVER a decision record: each limit name, baseline value + rationale, exchange-vs-local-cap decision + exact wire fields (byte order, bounds) if exchanged, the fail-closed behavior on limit breach (drop/reject, never unbounded), and validation-before-socket-use rules. Candidate-neutral, transport-agnostic. Feeds TASK-260715-2azda7 (schema/constants) and the relay UDP impl. If a value cannot be responsibly chosen without physical evidence, mark it an explicit M3 evidence gate with a safe M0 placeholder.
