.resources/TASK-260715-1vv52g/TASK-260715-1vv52g_approved-decision.md:1:STOP-THE-LINE RESOLVED (orchestrator, ADR-020). APPROVED: set HEV udp-copy-buffer-nums = 2 as an explicit INJECTABLE M0 baseline (Option 1 from the blocker doc). Rationale: HEV computes effective task stack = 20480 + max(tcp-buffer-size, 1500 x udp-copy-buffer-nums); the default 10 forces 35480, exceeding the 24576 low-mem target and the iOS memory budget (ADR-009). With udp-copy-buffer-nums=2, 1500x2=3000 <= tcp-buffer 4096, so effective task stack stays 24576. Keep udp-copy-buffer-nums INJECTABLE (do NOT hardcode a final value — M3 physical-UDP evidence gate). REJECTED: Option 2 (silently accept 35480 — understates memory planning, weakens AC2) and Option 3 (patch HEV — violates ADR-004 unmodified-source). NOW COMPLETE the integration per TASK-260715-1vv52g_inputs.md with this config so AC2 exact values hold (MTU recorded, UDP-in-TCP, task-stack 24576 via udp-copy-buffer-nums=2, tcp-buffer 4096, all injectable), satisfy AC1/3/4/5, and pass swift build + swift test. HEV stays unmodified.
.resources/TASK-260715-1vv52g/TASK-260715-1vv52g_blocker.md:19:Approve udp-copy-buffer-nums 2 as an explicit injectable M0 measurement input, with no HEV source patch. The exact required input is approval of that additional baseline value, or an explicit choice of option 2 or 3. Swift runtime wiring stopped before adding a compensating hidden constant.
