EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/TASK-260715-1q4qhw_record-vpn-configuration-lifecycle-contract/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped contract defines the exact owned-manager predicate and proves unrelated VPN managers are never edited or removed. 2. Save, reload, enable, permission, start, status observation, message, stop, host termination, and stale configuration flows have explicit outcomes and error mappings. 3. The provider remains the authority for runtime capability while NETunnelProviderSession remains the authority for system session state. 4. Start and stop completion-handler ownership, timeouts, cancellation, and idempotency are specified for both platforms. 5. The contract references the approved M0 identifiers and entitlements and reserves reconnect, fail-closed policy, and final UX for later milestones.
