codex
The architecture decision is now concrete: installation/update, enablement, session control, provider runtime, and cleanup are separate authority domains. In particular, enablement must be an explicit user-intent operation because Apple documents that enabling one enterprise VPN can disable another app’s enterprise VPN; ordinary “ensure configuration” must never do that implicitly. I’m recording this as both a contract rule and a board logbook finding.
